src/staking/PendlePT.sol:_initiateWithdraw:135|class=C21|High|_initiateWithdraw is gated only by require(PT.isExpired()) — a time check, never an authorization or solvency check — so it is the permissionless write that flips the caller's own position from the PT-priced branch to the escrow-priced branch, and because it performs external calls (_redeemPT → Pendle router / YT.redeemPY / SY.redeem, then withdrawRequestManager.initiateWithdraw) while t_CurrentAccount is still set, the branch can flip inside a transaction that has already passed a solvency check, and a reentrant read from the attacker-supplied router/limit-order callback returns the escrow number for an arbitrary caller-supplied shares that this file never clamps against w.sharesAmount.|src/staking/PendlePT.sol
